      <h2>About Jozani Chwaka Bay Nat. Park</h2>
      <div>Jozani Chwaka Bay National Park protects Zanzibar's last remaining indigenous forest and the endangered Zanzibar red colobus monkey (Procolobus kirkii), an endemic species found nowhere else on earth. Guided walks traverse mangrove boardwalks, coastal forest trails, and the Pete-Jozani mangrove corridor. Blue Sykes monkeys, lesser bushbabies, Ader's duiker, and over 50 bird species also inhabit the park. Entry fees directly fund conservation and community projects. Best visited early morning for wildlife activity.</div>
